# LeakSanitizer suppressions for third-party graphics/IPC libraries that leak during EGL initialisation
# (eglInitialize -> driver). Verified with fast_unwind_on_malloc=0 on the material tests: every reported stack starts in
# libEGL_nvidia/libnvidia-glsi/libdbus and the only project frame is main()'s eglInitialize call. A suppression hides a
# leak whenever one of these libraries is anywhere in its stack, so a project-owned GL object leaked inside a driver
# allocation would be hidden too; ASan itself (use-after-free, overflow) is unaffected.
leak:libEGL_nvidia
leak:libnvidia-glsi
leak:libnvidia-eglcore
leak:libdbus-1
leak:libEGL_mesa
leak:libgallium
leak:libgbm
